All tests pass.

**Root cause:** In `llm/llama_server.go`, both SSE stream parsers (completion loop at ~line 1511 and chat loop at ~line 1798) had a fallback that treated any line without a `data: ` prefix as a raw JSON event:

```go
evt, ok := bytes.CutPrefix(line, []byte("data: "))
if !ok {
    evt = line   // ping/comment lines like ":" hit this path
}
```

So SSE comment/ping lines (e.g. `:`) were passed straight to `json.Unmarshal`, failing with a bogus error.

**Fix:** Changed both fallbacks to `continue`, so non-data SSE lines (comments, pings) are ignored per the SSE spec:

```go
evt, ok := bytes.CutPrefix(line, []byte("data: "))
if !ok {
    // Skip SSE comment lines and other non-data lines (e.g. pings)
    continue
}
```

**Verification:** `go test ./llm/...` → `ok github.com/ollama/ollama/llm` (previously `TestLlamaServerCompletionSSEParsing` and `TestLlamaServerChatPromptEvalCountIncludesCache` failed).
